From 167a964fd25f3095343bd067c3476ef12aa9e800 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leo <leoschlosser@tutamail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:14:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 117/117] media: i2c: s5c73m3: power off even if the lens soft
 landing fails

When the soft landing of the lens failed, the OIF subdevice stayed
powered and its power count unchanged. With an ISP that doesn't answer
(a failed SPI boot, for one) the landing fails every time, so the
module was never powered off again, and every later open skipped the
ISP boot: the camera stayed dead until a reboot.

Report the failed landing and power off anyway.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/s5c73m3/s5c73m3-core.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/s5c73m3/s5c73m3-core.c b/drivers/media/i2c/s5c73m3/s5c73m3-core.c
index 9de9ea9f3..8a6a655be 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5c73m3/s5c73m3-core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5c73m3/s5c73m3-core.c
@@ -1448,11 +1448,10 @@ static int s5c73m3_oif_set_power(struct v4l2_subdev *sd, int on)
 			state->apply_fmt = 1;
 		}
 	} else if (state->power == !on) {
-		ret = s5c73m3_set_af_softlanding(state);
-		if (!ret)
-			ret = __s5c73m3_power_off(state);
-		else
+		/* A stuck ISP would never be booted again otherwise */
+		if (s5c73m3_set_af_softlanding(state))
 			v4l2_err(sd, "Soft landing lens failed\n");
+		ret = __s5c73m3_power_off(state);
 	}
 	if (!ret)
 		state->power += on ? 1 : -1;
-- 
